> A shorter feasible routing that greedy savings misses

Consider the six labelled points below, depot 0, unit customer demands and
capacity three. The heuristic returns routes [0,2,3,0] and [0,4,5,1,0], with
total length about 30.655229. The alternative routes [0,2,4,0] and [0,3,1,5,0]
serve the same customers at the same feasible loads and total about 30.520843.
This strict improvement is enough to disprove global optimality of the greedy
result. A development-test oracle also enumerates all customer permutations
and route cuts for this tiny problem and finds that same shorter minimum.
No exact optimization is implemented inside the report or production solver.

Native evaluate_vehicle_routes independently checks supplied route closure,
every customer occurrence, missing customers, repeated visits, interior depot
visits, capacity and consecutive-edge distance. In-range structural defects
return counts with feasible=false; invalid vertex ids and invalid original
problem data throw. The alternative is an explicit finite control, not a
general replacement solver. The diagram uses actual planar coordinates, with
the same scale in both panels; crossing line segments need not be route visits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/clarke_wright_counterexample.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<double,double>> points{{0,0},{2,-3},{-2,5},{0,-2},{4,1},{5,-4}};
  const std::vector<double> demand{0,1,1,1,1,1};
  const auto heuristic=dm::algorithms::clarke_wright_savings(points,demand,3);
  const std::vector<std::vector<std::size_t>> alternative{{0,2,4,0},{0,3,1,5,0}};
  dm::graphics::Diagram figure(60,1100);
  std::print("| routing | route | load | feasible whole routing | total length |\n| :--- | :--- | ---: | :--- | ---: |\n");
  for(int panel=0;panel<2;++panel) {
    const auto& routes=panel?alternative:heuristic.routes;
    const auto metrics=dm::algorithms::evaluate_vehicle_routes(points,demand,3,routes);
    if(!metrics.feasible)return 1;
    const double shift=11.0*panel;
    for(std::size_t r=0;r<routes.size();++r) {
      std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {} | {:.9f} |\n",panel?"shorter control":"greedy savings",routes[r],metrics.route_loads[r],metrics.feasible,metrics.total_distance);
      std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> path;
      for(const auto v:routes[r])path.push_back({points[v].first+shift,points[v].second});
      dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;stroke.width=2.8;stroke.color=r?dm::RGB{234,88,12}:dm::RGB{37,99,235};
      figure.path(path,stroke);
    }
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.circle=true;node.width=0.55;node.height=0.55;node.font_size=16;
    for(std::size_t v=0;v<points.size();++v) {
      node.fill=v?dm::RGB{255,255,255}:dm::RGB{254,240,138};
      figure.node(std::format("p{}_{}",panel,v),{points[v].first+shift,points[v].second},std::to_string(v),node);
    }
    figure.text({shift+1.5,7},panel?"shorter feasible control":"actual greedy routes",22)
          .text({shift+1.5,-6},std::format("length {:.6f}; loads {}",metrics.total_distance,metrics.route_loads),18);
  }
  figure.save_svg("build/clarke_wright_counterexample.svg");
  const auto shorter=dm::algorithms::evaluate_vehicle_routes(points,demand,3,alternative);
  if(heuristic.total_distance<=shorter.total_distance)return 1;
}
```
