> Capacity changes: measured routes, not a monotonicity theorem

Increasing capacity enlarges the feasible set, so the exact optimum cannot
increase. A greedy constructor can make different earlier choices, however;
that set-inclusion argument does not prove monotonicity of its returned length
or vehicle count. The next sweep reports actual outcomes on the same six
points. The horizontal orange line is the separate-trip star length,
measured by the native trace for every call.
It is a reference for this Euclidean example, not a global approximation bound.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/clarke_wright_capacity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<double,double>> points{{0,0},{2,-3},{-2,5},{0,-2},{4,1},{5,-4}};
  const std::vector<double> demand{0,1,1,1,1,1};
  std::vector<double> capacity,length,star;
  std::print("| capacity | returned vehicles | measured length | accepted merges | feasible |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(int cap=1;cap<=5;++cap) {
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::clarke_wright_trace(points,demand,cap);
    const auto metrics=dm::algorithms::evaluate_vehicle_routes(points,demand,cap,trace.result.routes);
    if(!metrics.feasible)return 1;
    capacity.push_back(cap);length.push_back(trace.result.total_distance);star.push_back(trace.initial_star_distance);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {} | {} |\n",cap,trace.result.routes.size(),trace.result.total_distance,trace.work.merges,metrics.feasible);
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(capacity,length,"returned",{37,99,235},2).points(capacity,length,"returned",{37,99,235},5)
      .line(capacity,star,"separate trips",{234,88,12},1.5)
      .legend({"greedy length","separate trips"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
      .title("Measured routing on one fixed Euclidean problem")
      .x_label("common vehicle capacity").y_label("total Euclidean route length")
      .x_limits(0.8,5.2).y_limits(0,50).save_svg("build/clarke_wright_capacity.svg");
}
