// result_end

Capacity comparison has no undocumented epsilon. Stored double literals 0.1 and
0.2 sum in widened arithmetic to slightly more than stored double 0.3, so those
two customer loads do not merge at that literal capacity. Integer demand units,
when natural to the application, make such boundaries easier to specify. NaNs,
infinities, negative demands, invalid depot ids and individually excessive
customer demands reject. Final costs outside finite double range throw; a
widened intermediate star can exceed that range when the merged result fits.

The seventeen new native tests pass address and undefined-behaviour sanitizers.
An independent deque-based route representation checks every sorted decision,
orientation, load, accepted order, final edge and named count across 1,926
line/depot/capacity cases and 1,000 seeded random Euclidean problems. Exhaustive
permutation-and-cut enumeration checks 100 additional small routing problems
and the fixed shorter-route control. Other cases cover exact and one-below
caps, validation before limits, zero demands, depot-only input, nonzero depot
ids, owned snapshots, malformed proposed routes and wide arithmetic. Synthetic
geometry suits these exact checks; no external dataset is needed here.

> What the analysis establishes

Savings joins preserve feasibility under the stated model and explain each
distance reduction in exact arithmetic. The native trace exposes actual
endpoint and capacity decisions, while independent route evaluation checks the
returned or proposed solution. Deterministic ordering and full validation make
the small examples repeatable, with bounded requested work. The six-point
control demonstrates the remaining optimization gap: feasible greedy routes
need not be the shortest routes.

> References

- G. Clarke and J. W. Wright (1964), *Scheduling of Vehicles from a Central Depot
  to a Number of Delivery Points*, Operations Research 12(4), 568–581,
  https://doi.org/10.1287/opre.12.4.568. The implementation follows the simple
  parallel savings variant with endpoint and capacity tests, rather than all
  possible extensions or improvement procedures.
- Canonical contracts and execution: include/datamunge/algorithms/clarke_wright.hpp
  and src/datamunge/algorithms/clarke_wright.cpp. The legacy tour_search.hpp
  include remains supported. All complete figure programs above are editable C++.
